# Derived from the inputs and rebuilt on demand: the downloaded recording, the
# extracted MusicXML, the engraved rows, the sync map, the preview stills.
build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Media, all of it. Nothing here is authored -- every recording is downloaded
# and every video is produced, song.json names the URL each one came from, and
# a render overwrites its one filename in place on every run. A scan of the
# sheet a score was transcribed from belongs to the same class: the notes it
# holds are in the .mxl, and no code reads the image.
#
# The only media this repo carries is the score itself, and a .mxl is kilobytes
# of zipped XML. If something here ever does need tracking, `git add -f` says
# so deliberately, which is the point.
*.mkv
*.mp4
*.webm
*.m4a
*.opus
*.wav
*.png
*.jpg

# MuseScore's own project file. The pipeline reads only the .mxl, and the
# editable score lives in MuseScore's cloud -- see score_source in song.json.
# Keeping a second copy here would be the mirror this repo deliberately avoids.
*.mscz

# The signed-in YouTube session, for videos the site will not serve anonymously.
# It belongs to the machine, not to the repo, and it is worth as much as the
# account password -- anyone holding it is signed in as you. Never commit it.
cookies.txt

# Console logs the Playwright MCP server drops wherever it happens to be run.
# They belong to a browsing session, not to a song or to the pipeline.
.playwright-mcp/
